# Docker

## Digest-pinned multi-stage pattern

Every Dockerfile uses a multi-stage build and digest-pinned bases. The
runtime stage runs as a non-root user. Builder may use root only if a
package install demands it.

Approved bases (see `02-supply-chain.mdc` for the canonical list and
the audit policy that depends on these strings):

| Purpose | Base |
|---|---|
| Python backend | `python:3.14-slim@sha256:...` |
| Node build stage | `node:24-alpine@sha256:...` |
| Static serve (built SPA) | `nginx:alpine@sha256:...` |
| Reverse proxy | `caddy:2-alpine@sha256:...` |
| Postgres (compose only) | `postgres:16-alpine@sha256:...` |

Bootstrap-time placeholder is `@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP`. Resolve
to a real digest with:

```bash
docker pull python:3.14-slim
docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' python:3.14-slim
```

…then commit the digest into the Dockerfile, `docker-compose.yml`, and
the image list inside `scripts/audit-all.sh`. The three must agree.

## Standard backend Dockerfile (Python + uv)

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM python:3.14-slim@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP AS builder
WORKDIR /app
ENV UV_LINK_MODE=copy \
    UV_COMPILE_BYTECODE=1 \
    UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/app/.venv \
    PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1

# uv from the official binary stage (also digest-pinned)
COPY --from=ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv:0.11.8@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP /uv /uvx /usr/local/bin/

COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock ./
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-install-project --no-dev

COPY . .
RUN uv sync --frozen --no-dev

FROM python:3.14-slim@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP
WORKDIR /app
ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:$PATH" \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
RUN useradd --create-home --uid 1000 app
COPY --from=builder --chown=app:app /app /app
USER app
EXPOSE 8000
ENTRYPOINT ["/app/.venv/bin/python", "-m", "uvicorn", "app.main:app", \
            "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]
```

## Standard frontend Dockerfile (Vue + pnpm + nginx)

```dockerfile
# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM node:24-alpine@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP AS builder
WORKDIR /app
RUN corepack enable && corepack prepare pnpm@9.15.0 --activate
COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml ./
RUN pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
COPY . .
RUN pnpm build

FROM nginx:alpine@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP
COPY --from=builder /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
EXPOSE 8080
```

(corepack is the cleanest way to pin pnpm on Node — no `npm install -g`
network round-trip and the version is explicit.)

## Caddy reverse proxy (optional, web template)

```dockerfile
FROM caddy:2-alpine@sha256:PIN_ME_AT_BOOTSTRAP
COPY Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
EXPOSE 80
```

The Caddyfile typically routes `/api/*` to backend, `/*` to frontend.

## .dockerignore is mandatory

Every Dockerfile has a sibling `.dockerignore`. At minimum:

```
.git
.venv
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.pnpm-store
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
```

## docker-compose.yml

Local development only — never used to deploy. Includes:
- App services with `build:` referencing the Dockerfile
- Postgres on `postgres:16-alpine@sha256:...` with a named volume
- Healthchecks on every service
- `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` for ordering
- Optional `proxy` service behind a Compose profile

## Forbidden

- Any `cgr.dev/chainguard/*` base (deprecated in this harness)
- Bare tags without `@sha256:` (e.g. `python:3.14-slim` alone)
- `USER root` in the runtime stage
- `ADD <url>` — use multi-stage with verified downloads
- `RUN curl ... | sh` — see `02-supply-chain.mdc`
- Building secrets into the image — use BuildKit `--mount=type=secret`
- Running the app as root in the runtime stage
